	<string id="job_try_give_sms">
		<text>A request from a stalker:</text>
	</string>
	<string id="job_try_give_sms_find">
		<text>find:</text>
	</string>
	<string id="job_try_give_1">
		<text>There's a job. We need to find -</text>
	</string>
	<string id="job_try_give_2">
		<text>Yeah, there's something. We need to find -</text>
	</string>
	<string id="job_try_has_1">
		<text>Did you find it yet? I need to -</text>
	</string>
	<string id="job_try_has_2">
		<text>Did you get it? This thing right here -</text>
	</string>
	<string id="oles">
		<text>Researcher.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="find_stancia_last_doc_desc">
		<text>It seems that the last, seventh part of the documents in Pripyat is missing. However, I got a message from Freedom that one of their groups went missing in the Chernobyl area, and they had a red folder with them - maybe that's what you need. We should try to find them in the vicinity of the power plant. According to Freedom, they were traveling in an APC.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="amet_dop_seif_raskaz">
		<text>Yeah, I heard that Rat gave you the keys to the old place. You're telling me to put another safe in there? Well, you can, of course. Only, I think you should understand some of the details. First of all, the safe itself - I remember there was one in some hut here near the Bar... let's say I put it together. The safe must have a lock that's in good working order, so that no one will steal anything, because here - people are clever and will do anything to get what they need or to get some quick cash. And most importantly, so that no one steals the safe, it should be magnetized to something so that it doesn't go anywhere. Magnetizing it against wall of the house would work, I'll tell you how. You know about the Magnet artifact, right? Only a few people know this: it has a specific property - if you stick it to something, it'll magnetize it, regardless of what it's made out of. Anyway, I'll help you, but I'll need 5,000 roubles for the job upfront. And I'll need four Magnet artifacts. Do you agree?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="enc_esc_evacuation">
		<text>Professor:\nThe group we were expecting is now in the Cordon, preparing to evacuate the area. Your job is to go there, and lead the group along the road through the highway to the exit of the area. I'm sending their coordinates, you'll get all the instructions when you get there. Hurry up. Over and out.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="mil_go_to_olmy_expedi_text">
		<text>Informant: Messer, one of the stalker squads has decided to move far into the Zone and explore Silent Hills. Among the squad's stalkers, more than half are elite. They were superbly equipped, can you go see what's wrong with them? Anything you find on them is yours. Just tell me what happened to them, alright? There were three stalkers in the group - two in exoskeletons, one was in a black protective suit, unless of course he'd changed costumes. I know for a fact he's a sniper. They went missing at the village. When you find them, contact me. I'll be waiting for the signal.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="jackal_podz">
		<text>Messer, here's the thing, Jackal's been in touch. He sent out an SOS signal. The message he sent was garbled in the transmission, he had something about some 'dark ones'. Bullshit .I spotted him underground in the Cordon area, obviously from the underground tunnels. Why don't you go check it out? You'll get to see each other face to face.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="space_start_tri_quest_article_name">
		<text>Professor Markov's order #3</text>
	</string>
	<string id="space_start_tri_quest_article_text">
		<text>Markov gave some kind of artifact. Near the Bar, a zombified stalker has reappeared in one of the apartment buildings. Markov offered me a job that'll kill two birds with one stone - get rid of a troublesome stalker, and conduct an experiment. We need to plant this artifact next to zombified stalker, which should disintegrate him.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="space_start_two_quest_article_name">
		<text>Professor Markov's order #2</text>
	</string>
	<string id="space_start_two_quest_article_text">
		<text>Markov did something with that artifact from the first order. Now we need to expose it to high temperatures.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="krvzovpobeg_name">
		<text>Major Kravtsov: My brother was forcibly drawn to the killers. He was forced to shoot another stalker, or they would have killed him themselves. There was nothing left for him to do. We need to find him, get him out of the killers' base, then bring him back to our base. Preferably at night, so no one can see you.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="killerdol_one_sttex">
		<text>Working for the Killers, that's new. Looks like the clan leader wants to cooperate? Then why are the others hostile? Too many questions. Nevertheless, you need to kill the stalker at the MedPribor Research Institute. He's hiding in the underground. The leader gave me a tip: the basement of the Research Institute can be accessed through the underground of the Garbage so you don't get too irradiated - the direct path to the MedPribor Research Institute's basement has dangerous levels of radiation.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="dolina_doki_bkoikr_desc">
		<text>We got a tip from Lone Wolf. He made it clear that they wouldn't just let me into the bar. We need to get some documents from the Dark Valley. This will be my fee for passing into the circle of experienced stalkers. There's some crazy psionic energy at the Dark Valley, we need protection. Lone Wolf told me about a special helmet you can get from the military, near the creek in the Garbage.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ratlab_strt_talk_haveart_name">
		<text>Toad's information about the lower levels of the Garbage</text>
	</string>
	<string id="ratlab_strt_talk_haveart_text">
		<text>According to Toad, he once saw a group of scientists in the Garbage a long time ago. They walked around, measured something, and went off toward the hangar, apparently into the basement rooms. Then, once under, the blowout hit them, and may still be lying there by the railway tunnel in a hole at the Garbage. Maybe I can find something from them that can open up access to the lower levels. You'll need an access code. Toad said that if I got in and found anything interesting and brought it to him, he will pay.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="agr_perepat_tainik_article_name">
		<text>The find in Strelok's stash</text>
	</string>
	<string id="agr_perepat_tainik_article_text">
		<text>Looks like we managed to find Strelok's stash, but it looks like there's nothing of value here... Found some book - it had a note in it that said where an PDA was stashed behind the main scientific complex of the MedPribor Research Institute in the basement. We should try to find it.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="check_gar_rat_cache">
		<text>Yeah, one more thing - there's a job. In that place, in the hangars, there's a passageway. There, deep underground, on the lower level of the tunnels, the stalkers discovered a large metal gate. Scans have confirmed that there are large rooms behind the gates. Come on, go downstairs and see what's going on. Report back to me later. I'm uploading any information about the entry point to those rooms into your PDA.</text>
	</string>
