	<string id="find_yaabneayb_1_article">
		<text>A request from the leader of Clear Sky</text>
	</string>
	<string id="bar_dolg_petrenko_start_21">
		<text>What do you want?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="taken_docs_vetri_pogo_prof_article_text">
		<text>Winds of Madness... what does it all mean? Anyway, apparently the road to the center of the Zone goes through Lake Yantar, and there's a certain scientist at Yantar - someone going by the nickname of Professor. He's the one who's going to have to help me with this, but I don't know if he'll want to help me. To get what I need, I'll have to work for Professor first.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pseudohuman_first_checkup_go_article_text">
		<text>Discovered a strange mutant. It looks like a meter maid, only more disfigured. Maybe we can find something interesting to do with this mutant. Something tells me this mutant isn't just a simple mindless goon, there's something else going on.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="rat_katacombs_quest_article_text">
		<text>We need to investigate the underground utilities beneath the Cordon. Before me, a group of stalkers had already disappeared there. You need to find some interesting thing for Toad from there and bring it to the Cordon.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="talk_docent_zamer_vibros_article_text">
		<text>Docent handed out a prototype of a device that protects your brain if you're exposed to a blowout without shelter. But, in order for him to finish his work, this prototype must be laid out in the open while a blowout is occuring. Doing this without any sort of protection is dangerous business.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="tips_jaba_bigcity">
		<text>This is the road to the Big City. It's closed now, the radiation levels are too high. That's where that radio program was from. You don't want to go that way right now.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="bunker_find_journl_fin_task_text">
		<text>The journalist is missing. I need to go north and find him, but first, we need to visit his apartment in Shining Path - Doctor gave us a tip-off: he used to live in Shining Path for a while, so I might be able to find something at where he used to live. Maybe I can find something.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="radar_deac_datel_1_task_text">
		<text>Everything seems ready for the trek north. The people from Duty should be waiting at Radar by now. My window of opportunity is from 9 PM to 11 PM.I need to break into the lab and shut down the Woodpecker before time runs out. After that, in theory, the road to Pripyat will be open.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="bar_dolg_propusk_taskt_text">
		<text>Next assignment from Toad: you need to find some kind of artifact on the tower that is at the railroad bridge and bring it to him. I need to remember to use the detector... damn, the battery in it is almost drained.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="strelby_pms_taskt_text">
		<text>Got the gun from Toad. It's in rough shape, but at least it's something. I have to go down the road, and then go to the underpass. There's a stalker waiting for me there, I think I'll need to take someone down with him, or something.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="doki_ploty_krisha_article_text">
		<text>Looks like another errand. On the roof of the factory, the Flesh that we've slaughtered has made a lair there. Toad says there are documents located there. We should find them and bring them to him. If I don't get the documents, he won't talk to me.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="komandir_kontr_article_text">
		<text>This is serious business - I need need to rescue the commander that was leading a patrol and get him to safety. He's located at the factory where the SOS signal is coming from. I need to check my gear and first aid kits, and a grenade from Toad would be nice.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="esc_find_glaz_zabiy_task_text">
		<text>After the recent emission, another Toad's Eye artifact appeared in the Garbage. I need to find it and bring it to Toad. He gave me the coordinates. I wonder why no one wants to go after it?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="esc_talk_dolg_garbage_task_text">
		<text>Toad sent me a message that says a stalker going by the nickname 'Boar' knows something about Strelok. He's located at the northern checkpoint at the Garbage - the one manned by Duty. I need to talk to him, and then go back to Toad. Toad also mentioned something about an eye artifact that Boar has, he wants it for whatever reason.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="jababoxone_task_text">
		<text>Damn, this sucks. Woke up in a strange place. That Toad is a very shady man. He wants me to work off what I owe him, fine. I need to pick up a crate from the bench in the merchant's bunker, and then take it to the roadblock. There's a crate containing something that Toad wants at the roadblock - the decoy crate should fool the grunts at the roadblock.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="esc_start_find_friend_task_text">
		<text>This is my first serious, real outing. I need to be well prepared. It's probably not a good idea to go alone, either. I need to try and find someone at the Cordon who will agree to go to the Research Institute with me. It's worth talking to the locals, see if anyone will agree. Well, if not, I guess I take my own chances.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="jurnwtf_hell645o_sms">
		<text>Talk to the leader of Duty</text>
	</string>
	<string id="jurnwtf_hel22lo_sms">
		<text>On my way out of Shining Path, I received a message from the leader of the Duty faction. I need to talk to him.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="article_find_gravimolot_text">
		<text>Informant sent me a message with a request. He wants me to find some kind of gravity-based device, supposedly made by some Burers, that's located somewhere within the basements of the MedPribor Research Institute some and bring it to him.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="article_bunker_2_olr_text">
		<text>Well, I guess the truth is out there. Now I can power down the mythical Black Monolith. I need to go down to the lower levels of the lab under Radar, and get to the control room of the installation. The lower door access code is 5489.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="article_yan_helieq_task_text">
		<text>I need to provide covering fire for the Yantar scientists that are leaving via helicopter. Professor gave some kind of rifle that must be returned after the mission is finished. Also, I can't go to the nearby village and attract attention to myself by shooting everything that moves - I'll have to do this quietly.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="article_poymat_plot_gm_text">
		<text>Professor gave me an assignment to catch a live Flesh specimen. How on earth am I going to do this? The hell he knows. It's probably gonna take a lot of running, Fleshes are fickle and cowardly creatures. According to these coordinates, there's a Flesh at one of the houses at Bright Beam.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="boots_start_gruz_task_text">
		<text>Professor said that a car with a load from the Big Land was driving to the mobile base. His radio communication with it was cut right at the entrance to the Exclusion Zone at the Cordon. I need to find the scientist and deliver the cargo to Professor. He didn't say anything about the cargo itself, but since his colleague was traveling by car, delivering the cargo on foot could be problematic.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="yan_food_dat_task_text">
		<text>The science bunker at Yantar is experiencing food supply problems. It's necessary to bring them food so I can continue to cooperate with them further. I think ten cans of food will be enough for them. It's worth talking to Toad, maybe he can sell large bulk orders of food.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="yan_spory_take_task_text">
		<text>Professor needs a measurement of air infected with spores from a certain parasite. In order to do this, I'll have to deploy this device given to me by Professor near any corpse infected with the parasite and then return it to him once it collects the data it needs.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="jghkkkjhhh">
		<text>When I was born, the Zone already existed. It's true, the old people said that there was a time that the town they lived in was outside the Zone, but I don't remember that. There are legends that somewhere there is some 'Big Land' or huge city, that's where the helicopters come from sometimes and the new stalkers come from. But something happened there a few years ago. Maybe the visiting stalkers know something more specific about this 'Big Land'.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="hfghfghgkkk">
		<text>Strelok, he also came from the outside, they say he was an important figure in the outside world, but nobody really knows anything. There were even rumors that fanatics from the Sin Clan believed that something important depended on him. Maybe he was thrice-born, too?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="hgfjmasrte">
		<text>Goplit knew something about him, we're from the same village. He always wanted to be a writer, he said he loved the fantasy genre. He's told me about heroes that always acted justly, and even if they were lonely, still defeated evil in the end. Goplit said something about the Journalist, the latter was looking for something, and Goplit bragged that he had found it - but whether he gave it to the Journalist or not, I don't know.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="gfdgdgdfgdfgdjgh">
		<text>Alright, don't ramble on, we'll get to your base, see what you accidentally grabbed. In the meantime, I should get something to eat, because I've forgotten when I've had anything in my mouth other than knocked out teeth. You didn't grab anything but folders in that archive?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="jurnwtf_hello_sms">
		<text>A journalist?!</text>
	</string>
	<string id="kiillde_about_arpop_und">
		<text>Hmmm.. I'm a business man. You're looking for Strelok, aren't you? I have information about him. If you do a job for me first, I'll tell you what I know about him - pro quid pro. Also, you're right about the radiation. But, that fugitive we're looking for is hiding in the basements of the research institute - there's no radiation there... I mean, in case you didn't know. The underground tunnels in the Garbage are connected to the MedPribor Research Institute underground, so if you go that way, you won't need the suit.. in theory. If you agree to do this, I'll give you information about the underground section of the MedPribor Institute.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="find_find_dezintegrator_article">
		<text>Searching for an unusual artifact</text>
	</string>
	<string id="dok_find_dezintegrator_article">
		<text>Some scientist on the roof of Bar asked me if it's possible to find this artifact. He only gave me a photo of it without any description or relevant information.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pda_btn_bloknot_hint">
		<text>A notebook with personal notes in it</text>
	</string>
	<string id="pda_btn_bloknot">
		<text>Notebook</text>
	</string>
	<string id="plen_quest_now_kick_article_name">
		<text>Jackal's note</text>
	</string>
	<string id="plen_quest_now_kick_article_desc">
		<text>The major's using everyone he can to find him. Killers... dark... The Doctor, his masterful work... put together a few pieces... We can't let the Major find him... you can't.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="osved_poisk_dokumentov">
		<text>I can help with that, but the result won't be immediate. You'll have to make inquiries, asking who's been where, when.. and one more thing. There are two options you can choose from.\nSo the first... if you give me two thousand roubles, I'll send you the approximate location of the document you're interested in a little while to your PDA.\nThe second option will cost you more: I'm the one who's pulling my strings and getting you the document you need. All you have to do is come and get it from me. It will cost more ten grand total. So, what do you need to find?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="off_yan1_none">
		<text>It's not working</text>
	</string>
	<string id="lvl_nightmare">
		<text>Unknown</text>
	</string>
	<string id="obmennakod">
		<text>Exchange for a code to the lab</text>
	</string>
	<string id="mertv_lead_ab_door_zakazz">
		<text>The leader of one of the bandit groups in the Dark Valley has agreed to give the password to enter the lab. In exchange for this information, he wants an VSK-94 rifle, and five bottles of vodka. If I can't get him five bottles of vodka, five jars will do. He also asked me to say hello to Informant at the Bar.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="zone_prosby">
		<text>Requests from other stalkers</text>
	</string>
	<string id="zone_zakazy">
		<text>Orders</text>
	</string>
	<string id="zone_sevenparts">
		<text>Found documents</text>
	</string>
	<string id="tip_use_door">
		<text>Open the door.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="enc_meat_coocked">
		<text>Cooked meat. This meat is entirely safe to eat.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="vorglaz_gig_talk1">
		<text>When the commotion started, I accidentally got into some room, they didn't lock a damn thing in there, they must have been sure no one would get in. There's some sort of archive, I took as many folders as I could fit into my duffel bag. I don't know why, but they're prized in the Zone. The Watchdog wouldn't let us trade information. Maybe he was dealing it himself. I can't understand the content of these papers, but you can sell them for good money, which means I'll be able to eat.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="barman_posr_talklong">
		<text>The mediator was generally unsociable, so I don't know about his affairs. He rarely came here, and if he did, he wasn't here for long. He was often seen at Yantar because he was testing something for the scientists there before. He came to the bar today, about an hour before his body was found. Before he died, he asked about all sorts of things - including questions about you.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="barman_posr_talklong2">
		<text>The last person who talked to him was Sanya Borov. Things weren't the warmest between them, you know. I once heard that the mediator ditched Sanya for some loot when they went to the Garbage. They just had another scandal today, and I had to kick them out. So far, all suspicions fall on Sanya, especially since he wanted to get away when he was found at the murder scene.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="barman_posr_talklong3">
		<text>Maybe someone's trying to cover their tracks by using your name. I think Khmyr was hanging around the table where Sanya was standing. Where he is now, I don't know. He left when the trouble started, which makes him suspicious. I should talk to the Informant about this. Hubby was just talking to him.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="barman_posr_talklong4">
		<text>I've been there, up north. I went through the Incinerator. I spent three days hiding from Monolith soldiers, in basements. Then back I went and got caught in a blowout. I've been hit by blowouts twice already, I'm all messed up. I've been told there's a clinic in the 'Big Land', where they treat this kind of thing, fixing your brain. Yet, here I am, I'm still alive.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="tutor_radiat_jornl_now_name">
		<text>Leaflet about radiation exposure</text>
	</string>
	<string id="tutor_radiat_jornl_now_desc">
		<text>Not all items found in the Zone of Alienation are safe. Weapons, food, artifacts, objects, everything can be exposed to radioactive contamination.\nAny individual object, even in a backpack, can absorb radiation if you enter an area that has heightened levels of background radiation. Be sure to carry a dosimeter or detector.\nWith a dosimeter, you can check if an object is contaminated. Just look it over in the backpack. If it's contaminated, the dosimeter will beep.\nNow, a little bit about radiation sickness.\nIt is possible to get radiation sickness by staying in areas with high levels of radioactive contamination, or by eating contaminated food. It'll manifest as a permanent decline in health and stamina. On top of that, your vision will get a yellowish haze. The worse the contamination, the higher the negative effects.\nIt can only be fought by taking large quantities of anti-rads, vodka, and some scientists seem to be able to cure this ailment.\nYou can keep an eye on the contamination rate by getting checked out by scientists. They may have already made some sort of diagnostic device.\nToad, 05/21/2007.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="esc_dead_kolodetz_article_text">
		<text>Messer, are you in the village right now? I need you to check out something for me: a hobo from the Garbage was bringing me a package from the Bar, but he disappeared somewhere around here. Look around and see if you can find him, or his package. If you find anything, bring it to me right away.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="dolg_hey_slez_ska">
		<text>What are you doing out there?</text>
	</string>
	<string id="voenstals">
		<text>Military stalkers</text>
	</string>
	<string id="reload_pda_now_desc">
		<text>Electrical supply data.\nData about the presence of a powerful source of electric generator directly behind the Chernobyl Nuclear Power Plant.\nThe data has been corrupted.\nBackup code for the entrance to the lower level of the energy center located in the underground segment of the facility at Radar- Data corrupted</text>
	</string>
	<string id="reload_pda_now_name">
		<text>Journalist's Message</text>
	</string>
	<string id="sl_x18_dream_name">
		<text>Strange dream</text>
	</string>
	<string id="sl_x18_dream_text">
		<text>I had a strange dream. The hulk of the Chernobyl plant, shrouded in darkness. Everything looks peaceful. A lone man appears. I can see him from the back against the power plant. The wind is starting to blow. Suddenly, a sea of rats starts scattering away from the power plant in different directions. A man standing with his back to me, shooting rats. Suddenly, the man in the dream shouts out "Strelok!". Then the man flinches, freezes for a moment and slowly starts to turn towards me, but I wake up the moment before I get to see his face What does this dream mean? I don't know, but I think it's something I've seen before.</text>
	</string>
	<string id="tip_use">
		<text>Use</text>
	</string>
